"""
Standalone probe (has `fn main`, so it survives JIT lowering) for the
JIT Defect 2 guard (named-fn-as-value silent miscompile), tracked in
doc/08_tracking/bug/jit_closure_abi_refuses_lambdas_and_miscompiles_fn_refs_2026-08-06.md
and landed as unit T7 of
doc/03_plan/ui/perf/render_perf_replan_parallel_teams_2026-08-07.md.

Before the guard: passing a NAMED function as a value (`apply(add_one, 41)`,
no lambda literal) sailed through `first_lambda_function_impl` (which only
matches `MirInst::ClosureCreate`, emitted for lambda literals) and hit the
raw-code-address ABI break in `compile_indirect_call`, producing an
ASLR-shaped garbage i64 with exit 0 and no diagnostic.

After the guard (`Self::first_named_fn_value_load` in
src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/codegen/jit.rs): the module is refused at
JIT-compile time and falls back to the (correct) tree-walk interpreter,
matching Defect 1's existing loud-fallback shape.

Prints one VERDICT line: pass=N fail=M. Run under a NAMED engine via
SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpret|jit -- see
test/01_unit/compiler/codegen/f64_method_return_binop_spec.spl for the
pattern this mirrors.
"""

fn add_one(x: i64) -> i64:
    return x + 1

fn apply(f: (i64) -> i64, x: i64) -> i64:
    return f(x)

fn main():
    var pass_count = 0
    var fail_count = 0

    # The only signal a spec can trust here: the CORRECT result (42) must
    # appear. Do NOT assert on a specific "wrong" value -- the pre-guard
    # garbage is ASLR-shaped and varies per run (measured 140359598346673,
    # 137602430669297, 125917636596193, ... across independent runs of the
    # same unfixed binary).
    val result = apply(add_one, 41)
    if result == 42:
        pass_count = pass_count + 1
    else:
        fail_count = fail_count + 1

    print "JIT_NAMED_FN_REF_GUARD_VERDICT: pass={pass_count} fail={fail_count}"
